            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Vinton Cerf</strong><br>\nVinton Cerf, often referred to as one of the \"fathers of the internet,\" was born in 1943 in New Haven, Connecticut. He was interested in technology from a young age and pursued his passion for electronics and computers through higher education.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Early Work</strong><br>\nCerf's educational background includes a bachelor's degree in mathematics from Stanford University and a master's and Ph.D. in computer science from UCLA. During his time at UCLA, he contributed to the development of the ARPANET, a precursor to the internet.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Development of TCP/IP</strong><br>\nVinton Cerf, along with Bob Kahn, is best known for developing the TCP/IP protocols, which are the foundation of internet data communication. Their work transformed the ARPANET into a global network, which became known as the internet.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Role in Expanding the Internet</strong><br>\nCerf's work did not stop with the creation of TCP/IP. He has played a key role in the expansion of the internet, advocating for its growth and the establishment of new technologies and policies to ensure its accessibility.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Internet Governance</strong><br>\nCerf has been involved in the governance of the internet, helping to set up institutions that manage domain names and internet standards. His leadership in organizations like ICANN has been critical in shaping the internet's infrastructure.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Awards and Honors</strong><br>\nFor his work, Cerf has received numerous accolades, including the Presidential Medal of Freedom and the Turing Award. These honors recognize his contributions to computer science and the transformative impact of his work on modern communication.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
